            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>Even the smallest house spirits can band together against a threat to the home.</p><hr /><p>House spirits are a collection of fey who live among peasants and poor rural folk. They hide themselves from mortal eyes—hence why they're so commonly called \"spirits\"—but their presence is always felt. Given suitable respect, these house fey take a decidedly parental interest in the mortals they live with, doing all manner of work around the household. They cook, they clean, they sweep, they chop wood, they care for animals, they tend the stove. If disrespected, however, they becomes a veritable plague of ill will.</p>",
            "publication": {
